{
  "voice": "成人男声｜老师清晰",
  "reference": "/Users/zhaozixu/Documents/Codex/2026-06-04/new-chat/work/full_voice_catalog/12-adult-male-teacher-clear.wav",
  "cfg_value": 1.35,
  "inference_timesteps": 12,
  "normalize": false,
  "sentence_method": "one complete sentence per generation",
  "word_method": "independent word generation, not extracted from sentence audio",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "It's always a good thing to have a hobby, such as collecting stamps or baking.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-01.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "For Miss Patty, a school bus driver, her hobby of knitting has made her really touch the community.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-02.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Miss Patty always wanted to do something in her spare time to help the students.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-03.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After a conversation with one of the students, things took a turn from knitting one hat to knitting more hats.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-04.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The boy in the school uniform gets on the bus, and he goes, 'What are you doing?'",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-05.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "I said, 'I'm making a hat.'",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-06.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "He said, 'That would be great having such a warm hat in icy winter.'",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-07.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "So I said, 'What colour would you like?'",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-08.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "That started everything.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-09.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "Miss Patty told the local newspaper.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-10.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "Several years have passed since that day, and Miss Patty has already knitted 7,083 hats, along with some gloves for students.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-11.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "Sometimes she will get the student's favourite colour before she begins the project.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-12.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "What is more moving is that Miss Patty buys all the materials using her own cash.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-13.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "Some people do give her gift cards around the Christmas holidays to help, but she still withdraws a lot of dollars from her own bank account.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-14.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "She also manages her time well to keep her kitchen and bedroom tidy and even to visit the local museum for inspiration.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-15.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "Along with the charity act of making pretty hats for the students, that will keep them warm.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-16.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "Miss Patty also gets praise for being a trusted friend to the students.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-17.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "text": "Of course, the kids can buy hats from a store, but they always like hers better.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-18.mp3",
      "exists": true
    }
  ],
